<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.2.2: Standard and Factored Forms of Perfect Squares</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02351</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.2.2: Standard and Factored Forms of Perfect Squares</md:title>
    <md:uuid>651297ce-349c-4071-a4dc-6540d46e25de</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">      <title>Activity</title>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00001">What is the factored form of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          <para id="para-00002">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00004"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00005">What is the factored form of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          <para id="para-00006">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00008"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00009">What is the standard form of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          <para id="para-00010">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00011">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00012"><m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>14</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>49</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_192cf81b-d5a2-40e1-8371-c1dc947f33fe" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00013">Enter the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00014">What is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00015">Correct! 100</para>
          <para id="para-00016">The correct answer is 100.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_54de037c-cf37-4094-a566-86908cd0c14f" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00017">Enter the missing value of the factored form.</para>
          <para id="para-00018">If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is factored to be <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the missing value of the factored form of this expression?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00019">Correct! 10</para>
          <para id="para-00020">The correct answer is 10.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="a9b00ee4-f9d9-4f3f-887a-15186f558c2b" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00021">Enter the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00022">What is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00023">Correct! 64</para>
          <para id="para-00024">The correct answer is 64.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_3d0250f2-4dbd-43fe-924d-38870521d864" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00025">Enter the missing value of the factored form.</para>
          <para id="para-00026">If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is factored to be <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the missing value of the factored form of this expression?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00027">Correct! 8</para>
          <para id="para-00028">The correct answer is 8.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00029">What is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          <para id="para-00030">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00031">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00032"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>49</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00005">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00033">If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is factored to be <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the missing value of the factored form of this expression?</para>
          <para id="para-00034">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00035">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00036"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00006">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          <para id="para-00037">What is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          <para id="para-00038">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">
          <para id="para-00039">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00040"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00007">
        <problem id="prob-00011">
          <para id="para-00041">If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is factored to be <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the missing value of the factored form of this expression?</para>
          <para id="para-00042">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00011">
          <para id="para-00043">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00044"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <para id="para-00045">Notice that finding the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> helped to create a <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00001">perfect square trinomial</term>. This is called <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00002">completing the square</term>.</para>
    </section>
    <note id="note-00001">
      <title>Building Character: Intellectual Humility</title>
    <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
          <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_10_04_03_01.png"/>
        </media>
      <para id="para-00046">When you approach life with intellectual humility, you open your mind to learning. You are able to learn from opposing views and have more constructive discussions, even when you disagree.</para>
      <para id="para-00047">Think about yourself. Are these statements true for you?</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>I question my own opinions, positions, and viewpoints because they could be wrong. </item>
        <item>In the face of conflicting evidence, I am open to changing my opinions. </item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00048">Don’t worry if none of these statements are true for you. Developing this trait takes time. Your first step starts today!</para>
    </note>
    <note class="self-check" id="note-00002">
      <exercise id="exer-00009">
        <problem id="prob-00013">
        <para id="para-00049"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_9_2_2_SC"/></para>
        </problem>
        </exercise>       
    </note>
    <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>
      <section id="sect-00003">
        <title>Completing the Square</title>
        <para id="para-00050">When a number is added to a <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00003">quadratic expression</term> to make a <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00004">perfect square trinomial</term>, that is called <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00005">completing the square</term>.</para>
        <para id="para-00051">Here is how to complete the square of a quadratic expression, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        <note id="note-00003">
          <title>How to Complete a Square of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></title>
          <para id="para-00053"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Identify <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, the coefficient of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00054"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Find half of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and then square it. In other words, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00055"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Add the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00056"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - Factor the perfect square trinomial, writing it as a binomial squared.</para>
        </note>
        <para id="para-00057"><emphasis>Example</emphasis></para>
        <para id="para-00058">Complete the square to make a <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00006">perfect square trinomial</term>. Then write the result as a binomial squared.</para>
        <para id="para-00059"><m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>26</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00060"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Identify <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, the coefficient of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. </para><para id="para-00072">The coefficient of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is -26.</para>
        <para id="para-00061"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Find half of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and then square it. In other words, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>. </para><para id="para-00073"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>26</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>13</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>169</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00062"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Add the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. </para><para id="para-00074"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>26</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>169</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00063"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - Factor the perfect square trinomial, writing it as a binomial squared. </para><para id="para-00075"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>13</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <note class="try" id="note-00004">
          <title>Try It: Completing the Square</title>
          
            <exercise id="exer-00008">
              <problem id="prob-00012">
                <para id="para-00064">Complete the square to make a <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00007">perfect square trinomial</term>. Then, factor the trinomial.</para>
                <para id="para-00065"><m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mi>_</m:mi><m:mi>_</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00066">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
              </problem>
              <solution id="sol-00012">
                <para id="para-00067">Here is how to complete the square.</para>
                <para id="para-00068"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Identify the coefficient of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. </para><para id="para-00076"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                <para id="para-00069"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Find <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>. </para><para id="para-00077"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                <para id="para-00070"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Add the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> to the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. </para><para id="para-00078"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                <para id="para-00071"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - Factor the perfect square trinomial. </para><para id="para-00079"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
              </solution>
            </exercise>
          </note>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>